      "title": "GitHub introduces Agent Host Protocol for cross-device agent sessions",
      "summary": "GitHub introduced the open Agent Host Protocol to maintain agent sessions across editors, mobile applications, desktop software, and cloud environments. The standard preserves execution context across platforms so users can switch devices without losing active tasks.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Open protocol keeps agent sessions synchronized across editors, mobile, and cloud.",
        "Preserves execution state and context during cross-device platform handoffs."
      ],
      "design_implication": "A designer managing an autonomous workflow often loses context when switching from a desktop environment to a phone. With session continuity standardized across surfaces, interfaces no longer need bespoke sync logic to resume multi-step agent actions. Audit handoff flows across platforms to ensure mobile and desktop surfaces present identical progress checkpoints, permissions, and cancel controls.",
