      "title": "Multimodal LLM text explanations increase perceived trust in XAI visualizations",
      "summary": "Researchers evaluated whether augmenting explainable AI visualizations with textual descriptions generated by multimodal language models improves user comprehension. The pre-registered study found that pairing visual model outputs with generated natural-language explanations significantly improved perceived understanding and trust.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Evaluates multimodal language model explanations paired with complex XAI visualizations.",
        "Pre-registered study measured effects on perceived understanding and user trust.",
        "Textual descriptions significantly improved interpretation of difficult model outputs."
      ],
      "design_implication": "In high-stakes dashboards, users frequently abandon complex model visualizations because feature importance charts remain difficult to interpret alone. Augmenting visual evidence with concise, natural-language summaries bridges comprehension gaps without cluttering the display. Pair dense algorithmic charts with plain-text interpretations explaining which factors influenced the decision and why.",
